    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following the rules in `spec.md`, keeping the given signature and the `CouponError` class. Coupon checks run in spec order: expiry, used code, minimum subtotal, then kind, after which the percent/fixed value bounds are checked. Shipping is computed on the post-discount subtotal, and an empty item list has no shipping. The result is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 36 pytest cases covering the validation errors, coupon boundaries (expiry day, minimum subtotal, 100% percent, fixed discount capped at the subtotal), shipping thresholds, and rounding. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 36. Two of my first-run expectations were wrong (a 10% coupon on 100.00 leaves 90.00, which incurs shipping, so the total is 100.00); I corrected the tests, not the implementation. I did not run a coverage measurement, since the command allowed here is only the test run. Every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by a test, so I expect the 90% coverage gate to pass, but that is unverified.",
